Well, Magicbane is perhaps not the best example because it _can_ be
generated as a random object in the dungeon.  Therefore with enough
time, a wishless atheist hero could acquire Magicbane without bones.

But consider *DSM (pre-astral plane) or quest artifacts, I'd say that
in a game with conducts that allowed for a means of acquiring such
items without bones (through scrolls or wishing) then picking up
someone else's *DSM or Quest Artifact wouldn't be a case of
extraordinary luck.  Just the same as picking up someone's potions of
healing wouldn't be out of the norm, since finding the bones didn't
exclusively allow for the existence of the object, it only made it
happen at that location and perhaps much earlier in the game.

But, I just realized something: the player monsters on Astral are
often wearing highly enchanted armor and DSM in particular!  I might
